{"name":"Promised Amethyst","hex":"#686278","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"promised","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Predicted; expected; anticipated.","Under obligation to some future commitment, such as a marriage or vocation."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of promise"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/promised"},{"term":"amethyst","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A transparent purple to violet variety of quartz with traces of manganese, used as a gemstone.","A purple colour."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour similar to that of the gemstone"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/amethyst"}],"entries":[{"title":"Promise","blocks":[{"text":"A promise is a commitment by someone to do or not do something. As a noun promise means a declaration assuring that one will or will not do something. As a verb it means to commit oneself by a promise to do or give. It can also mean a capacity for good, similar to a value that is to be realized in the near future."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Promise","wikidata":"Q1425577"},{"title":"Amethyst","blocks":[{"text":"Amethyst is a violet variety of natural quartz. Ancient Greeks wore amethyst and carved drinking vessels from it in the belief that it would prevent intoxication. Amethyst, a semiprecious stone, is often used in jewelry. It occurs mostly in association with calcite, quartz, smoky quartz, hematite, pyrite, fluorite, goethite, agate, and chalcedony."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Amatista_Laye_2.jpg/330px-Amatista_Laye_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amethyst","wikidata":"Q79058"},{"title":"Lavender (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lavender is a light shade of purple or violet. It applies particularly to the color of the flower of the same name."}],"image":"http